                    "text": "param dry_wet_mix 0.5 @min 0 @max 1",
                    "varname": "dry_wet_mix"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-37",
                    "linecount": 71,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 577.0, 1043.0 ],
                    "text": "================================================================================\nchorus_bbd_compander_juno — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nOVERVIEW\nA standalone stereo analog Bucket-Brigade Device (BBD) Chorus uniting three DAFx virtual-analog papers:\n1. Antti Huovilainen (DAFx-05 Paper P_155, Sections 5.1 & 5.2, Eq. 25–31, Fig. 8–11): Models the fixed-bucket-count variable-clock delay law (where a linear triangle LFO warps into an asymmetric 1/f_clock hyperbola smoothed by the bucket transit time, Eq. 25) and the matched NE570 2:1 feedback compressor / 1:2 feedforward expander.\n2. Colin Raffel and Julius O. Smith (DAFx-10 Paper P42, Sections 2.2, 3.3 & 4.4): Models clock-tracking Sallen-Key anti-aliasing and reconstruction lowpass filters plus stage-accumulated MOSFET charge-transfer harmonic warmth.\n3. Martin Holters and Julian D. Parker (DAFx-18 Paper 12, Sections 2 & 4): Models the classic Roland Juno-60 / Dimension-D push-pull stereo BBD chorus architecture (Mode I, Mode II, and Dual I+II).\n\nINLETS & OUTLETS\n- in1 / in2: Stereo Audio Input (Tuba; mono in1 auto-normalizes to stereo)\n- in3: Unused / Thru (standalone chorus requires no external pitch tracker)\n- in4: Optional 1-Bar Audio-Rate Phasor [0..1] (syncs primary BBD triangle LFO to host tempo when patched)\n- out1 / out2: Stereo Analog BBD Chorus Output\n\nPARAMETERS (7)\n\n1. lfo_rate_hz\n   - Range: 0.10 to 5.00 Hz (Primary BBD Triangle LFO Rate, Default: 0.55 Hz, matching Roland Juno-60 Mode I = 0.51 Hz / Mode II = 0.86 Hz)\n   - Taper: Direct frequency in Hz.\n   - Function: Sets the sweep speed of the BBD clock generator.\n\n2. clock_mod_depth\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (BBD Clock Frequency Modulation Depth, Default: 0.60)\n   - Taper: Linear clock modulation index (warped via 1 / (1 + m*LFO) per Huovilainen DAFx-05 Fig. 9).\n   - Function: Controls the excursion of the variable BBD clock, producing warm, asymmetrical pitch thickening.\n\n3. center_delay_ms\n   - Range: 1.50 to 15.00 ms (Nominal MN3007 512-Stage BBD Delay Time, Default: 3.60 ms, matching the Juno-60's 3.45 ms center delay)\n   - Taper: Direct delay time in milliseconds (determines nominal clock frequency f_clock = 512 / (2 * delay)).\n   - Function: Short delays (1.5–4.0 ms) deliver tight Roland Juno/Dimension-D stereo widening; longer delays (6–15 ms) produce lush 1970s Boss CE-1 ensemble doubling.\n\n4. juno_mode_morph\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (Default: 0.35)\n   - Taper: Continuous morph between:\n     * 0.0: Pure Push-Pull Anti-Phase Triangle LFO (Juno Mode I / Dimension-D spatial widening with zero mono pitch wobble)\n     * 1.0: Dual-Rate Incommensurate LFO Sum (Juno I+II multi-voice ensemble swirl)\n   - Function: Morphs the modulation law from single-LFO push-pull stereo to dual-LFO ensemble movement.\n\n5. ne570_compand\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (NE570 Compander Depth, Default: 0.55)\n   - Taper: Linear wet/dry blend of the 2:1 feedback compressor before the BBD and 1:2 feedforward expander after the BBD (DAFx-05 Eq. 26–27).\n   - Function: Reproduces the dynamic \"breathing\" and transient punch of analog BBD pedals equipped with Philips NE570/SA571 compander ICs.\n\n6. bbd_warmth_thd\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (BBD Sallen-Key Roll-Off & MOSFET Charge-Transfer THD, Default: 0.45)\n   - Taper: Linear warmth control.\n   - Function: Simultaneously darkens the clock-tracking anti-aliasing/reconstruction lowpass filters and increases asymmetrical bucket-stage harmonic saturation (DAFx-10 Sec 4.4).\n\n7. dry_wet_mix\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (0% Dry to 100% Wet Vibrato; Default: 0.50 = Classic 50/50 Stereo Chorus)\n   - Taper: Constant-power cosine/sine crossfade.\n   - Function: At 0.50, creates full stereo BBD chorusing; at 1.00, isolates the wet BBD path for true pitch vibrato.\n",
                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                }
            }
        ],
